# Repo-specific privacy patterns for homelab-mcp, one extended-regex per line.
# The shared scripts/check_privacy.sh already covers internal host names, real
# IPs, emails and dated prose. These add what is specific to this repo: a
# config/tool server that talks to real infrastructure, so the danger is a
# real endpoint URL or SSH alias slipping into an example or a fixture.
#
# All examples and fixtures must use .invalid / .example hostnames and the
# RFC 5737 documentation IP ranges only.

# Real SSH aliases / host shortnames from the author's environment.
\b(pve-g3|ct-20[0-9]|ct-21[0-9]|ct-212|nanopi|ai-host|ha-green)\b

# Internal DNS suffixes.
\.lan\b|\.local\b|\.home\b|\.internal\b

# Real endpoint hints — a non-.invalid grafana/netbox/influx/proxmox URL.
https?://[a-z0-9.-]*\.(?!invalid|example)[a-z]{2,}[:/][^ "']*\b(grafana|netbox|influx|pve|proxmox|adguard)
